\f0\fs24 \cf2 <$Scr_Ps::0>
\f1\fs22 Security at HIBReLabs had been designed by people who assumed theft would involve terabytes, industrial espionage or someone with a pallet jack and a fake moustache. Also, there had never been a security breach in the history of the lab. Two vials leaving in the possession of Dr Janine Anstey, or patient samples coming back, did not trouble the routine-numbed imaginations of security personnel. Modesty forbids us to describe where she put them, but we will tell you she had a portable fridge in her car.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
<!$Scr_Ps::0><$Scr_Ps::1>
\f1\fs22 Dr Hermann took his lunch break. With any luck, he might sneak back to the small dormitory and take a light nap. Apparently it improved his creativity and alertness.\
Anstey waited until Hermann disappeared down the corridor, then took a muscle biopsy from a drawer of an unused desk, and carried it through to sequencing. The workstation recognised her credentials, and woke the sequencer. She prepared the tissue, isolated the DNA and loaded the sample.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0
\cf2 When the run was complete, Anstey found the TPlus Master Construct record and dragged it onto the detail window of the sample. A dialogue box popped up; she selected 
\f2\b\fs20 FIND HOST JUNCTIONS.
\f1\b0\fs22 \
The workstation binged and threw the result onto the holoscreen. The Master Construct hung on the left. On the right, human chromosome ran into TPlus, matched the construct from end to end, then became human again.\
Anstey enlarged the alignment and rotated in the air above the workstation. There it was, the whole thing. TPlus.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0
\cf2 Hermann was wrong; TPlus could achieve sustained integration under at least one profile. There it was, the complete construct, present inside a chromosome.\
Anstey savoured the onscreen results until her eyes watered. \
The bloods had remained clean through every treatment. TPlus had reached the circulation, but never anywhere near Hermann\'92s toxic range. Moreover, the circulating level had stopped falling as his model said it should.\
TPlus was the elixir for longer, healthier life. You just had to start with muscular dystrophy first.\
Anstey reflected on the danger she was still in, but she smiled anyway.\
Pin Cushion would need to adopt a new nickname.
